(YOUR 30-SECOND PITCH) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(My project evaluates an inverse-kinematics-assisted Deep Q-Network for) Tj
0 -14 Td
(target-reaching) Tj
0 -14 Td
(and simulated energy use in a PyBullet KUKA iiwa. I compared a selected greedy DQN) Tj
0 -14 Td
(checkpoint with a fixed-speed inverse-kinematics baseline on the same 50 held-out) Tj
0 -14 Td
(seeds. The DQN reached 44 targets and the baseline reached 45. Among 44 seeds where) Tj
0 -14 Td
(both succeeded, the DQN used 10.82% more energy on average. So target reaching was) Tj
0 -14 Td
(demonstrated in simulation, but energy saving was not. The main next step is to) Tj
0 -14 Td
(improve the energy objective and repeat evaluation across several training seeds.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(YOUR 2-MINUTE STORY) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(1. Problem: Robot controllers must complete work while managing energy. Reward) Tj
0 -14 Td
(design) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   can create a trade-off between task completion and energy cost.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(2. Aim: Test whether an IK-assisted DQN can reach targets while reducing simulated) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   grid energy compared with a simple fixed-speed IK controller.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(3. Setup: PyBullet simulation of a KUKA iiwa. Six joints were controlled and the) Tj
0 -14 Td
(wrist) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   roll was locked. Each observation had 23 values; the DQN chose from 89 discrete) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   actions. Episodes had two target phases and a 200-step limit.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(4. Energy model: Positive simulated mechanical work counted as grid draw. Simulated) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   braking work could charge a 50 Ws buffer at 80% efficiency for later use.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(5. Evaluation: The selected greedy checkpoint and IK baseline were run on the same) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   50 held-out seeds, 1000 to 1049. Energy comparisons used only shared successes.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(6. Finding: DQN success was 88% and IK success was 90%. On matched successes, the) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   DQN energy saving was minus 10.82%; a negative value means DQN used more energy.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(7. Conclusion: The result validates target reaching for this selected simulation) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   checkpoint, but does not validate the energy-saving objective.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(MEMORIZE THESE NUMBERS) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(DQN held-out completion: 44/50 = 88%. IK held-out completion: 45/50 = 90%.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Matched successful episodes: 44. Mean paired energy saving: -10.82%. Mean peak) Tj
0 -14 Td
(reduction: 0.22%; median peak reduction: 3.24%. Separate online history: 3 successes) Tj
0 -14 Td
(in 500 episodes = 0.6%. Do not merge the two evaluation phases.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(Sources: project results/colab_run_2026-11-24/verified_evaluation_summary.csv,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(paired_evaluation.csv, training_history.csv, and README.md.) Tj
