(METHOD AND TERMS) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -30 Td
(DQN: A value-based reinforcement-learning method. A neural network estimates the) Tj
0 -23 Td
(value of each discrete action for a given state; the agent selects actions using) Tj
0 -14 Td
(epsilon-greedy exploration during training.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(IK: Inverse kinematics maps a desired end-effector position to joint configurations.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(In this project, IK demonstrations warm-start the learned controller. The baseline) Tj
0 -14 Td
(uses fixed-speed IK; the tested DQN is not learning from scratch.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(Replay buffer: Stores past state, action, reward, next-state, and done transitions.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Training samples batches from this memory to update the Q network.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(Target network: A delayed copy of the Q network used to stabilize learning targets.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(Held-out seeds: Random seeds reserved for evaluation rather than the training run.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Here, both controllers were evaluated using the same 50 seeds \(1000-1049\).) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(Matched successes: Seeds where both the DQN and IK baseline completed the task. The) Tj
0 -14 Td
(paired energy comparison uses these 44 seeds, making the comparison more meaningful) Tj
0 -14 Td
(than comparing each controller's energy over different sets of successful episodes.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(ENERGY RESULT - SAY IT PRECISELY) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(The project reports mean per-seed energy saving of -10.82% for 44 matched successful) Tj
0 -14 Td
(episodes. The sign convention is baseline energy minus DQN energy, divided by) Tj
0 -14 Td
(baseline) Tj
0 -14 Td
(energy. A negative result means the DQN consumed more energy on average. Do not) Tj
0 -14 Td
(claim) Tj
0 -14 Td
(that the DQN reduced energy. The 0.22% mean peak reduction is small; the 3.24%) Tj
0 -14 Td
(median) Tj
0 -14 Td
(peak reduction does not change the negative mean energy result.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(WHY 3/500 AND 44/50 BOTH APPEAR) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(3/500 is the online training history's success count. 44/50 is a separate greedy) Tj
0 -14 Td
(evaluation of the selected IK-warm-started teacher checkpoint on held-out seeds.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(They) Tj
0 -14 Td
(are different phases, policies, and datasets. The later evaluation does not mean the) Tj
0 -14 Td
(training run itself achieved 88% success, and it should not be described that way.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(LIMITATIONS TO STATE BEFORE THE PANEL ASKS) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(- This is a simulation; no physical KUKA robot was tested.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- The buffer and energy calculation are simplified, not calibrated against motor,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(  battery, or factory power measurements.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- The comparison uses one selected checkpoint and 50 held-out seeds.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Energy results are conditional on both controllers completing the same seed.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Findings describe this prototype and setup, not all industrial robots.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(Sources: Li, Liu, and Dong \(2022\), DOI 10.1109/TII.2021.3125447; Peri et al. \(2025\),) Tj
0 -14 Td
(PMLR 305, https://proceedings.mlr.press/v305/peri25a.html.) Tj
0 -14 Td
ET
