/F1 18 Tf
(LIKELY PANEL QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -30 Td
(Q: What is the main contribution of the project?) Tj
0 -23 Td
(A: It builds and evaluates an IK-assisted DQN pipeline with a simulated energy) Tj
0 -14 Td
(buffer,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(then compares target completion and energy against a fixed-speed IK baseline on) Tj
0 -14 Td
(shared) Tj
0 -14 Td
(held-out seeds. The measured result includes a negative energy finding.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(Q: Did the DQN improve energy efficiency?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(A: No. In the 44 matched successful episodes, mean paired energy saving was -10.82%.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(With the project's sign convention, that means the DQN used more energy on average.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(Q: Then was the project successful?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(A: The evaluation produced a reproducible comparison and identified that the energy) Tj
0 -14 Td
(objective was not met by this selected checkpoint. I should not present that as) Tj
0 -14 Td
(energy) Tj
0 -14 Td
(improvement. The scientific result is an honest measurement and a clear next step.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(Q: Why is the held-out DQN result 88% if online training was 0.6%?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(A: Those figures describe separate phases. The 0.6% is online training history. The) Tj
0 -14 Td
(88% is a greedy evaluation of the selected checkpoint that had been warm-started) Tj
0 -14 Td
(with) Tj
0 -14 Td
(IK demonstrations, on 50 held-out seeds. They are not directly interchangeable.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(Q: Why use IK demonstrations?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(A: The initial online DQN learning was weak. IK demonstrations give a starting) Tj
0 -14 Td
(policy) Tj
0 -14 Td
(for a difficult robot-control task. The evaluation is therefore of an IK-assisted) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(DQN,) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf
(not a DQN that learned the task entirely without prior demonstrations.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(Q: Why compare only 44 seeds for energy?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(A: Those are the seeds on which both controllers completed. Comparing energy on) Tj
0 -14 Td
(different success sets could be misleading because task completion affects energy.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(The 44-seed result is conditional on both controllers succeeding.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(Q: What does the 50 Ws buffer represent?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(A: It is a simulated storage capacity in watt-seconds. The model allows a portion of) Tj
0 -14 Td
(simulated braking work to be recovered and used later. It is an assumption in the) Tj
0 -14 Td
(simulation, not a physical battery test.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(Q: Why does the reward not guarantee energy saving?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(A: Reward weights create a trade-off. The policy can prioritize task progress or) Tj
0 -14 Td
(completion over energy cost. The evaluation shows why energy and completion need to) Tj
0 -14 Td
(be reported separately and why reward design needs further study.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(Q: Is the KUKA iiwa a seven-joint robot? Why do you say six joints?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(A: PyBullet's model has seven physical joints. This environment controls six and) Tj
0 -14 Td
(locks) Tj
0 -14 Td
(the wrist-roll joint. That is why the state/action design refers to six controlled) Tj
0 -14 Td
(joints.) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -8 Td
(Q: Can these results be generalized to factory robots?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(A: No. They are simulation results using simplified energy accounting. Physical) Tj
0 -14 Td
(validation and calibrated power measurements would be needed for that claim.) Tj
0 -14 Td
ET
endstream
